# Driver file version

Each `configs/*.json` file owns a top-level `"version"` (`major.minor.patch`). That value is independent of `package.json` and of every other config in this module.

## When editing a driver

- Change only the files whose protocol, CAT, serial, memory, or capabilities actually change.
- Bump `"version"` in each changed file in the same edit.
- Leave unchanged sibling configs (and their versions) untouched.
- Do not copy the module or `package.json` version onto configs.
- Do not run `stamp-config-versions` or otherwise rewrite every config to one version.

## How to bump

| Change | Bump |
| --- | --- |
| New radio config | Start at `1.0.0` |
| Compatible addition (new optional CAT field, extra baud rate) | minor |
| Compatible fix (wrong expect byte, corrected skip range) | patch |
| Incompatible protocol or layout change | major |

Example: a UV-5R protocol fix bumps `baofeng-uv5r.json` from `3.1.1` to `3.1.2`. A later sibling config must keep its own version and must not be rewritten to match `package.json`.
